e firm also launches equity, commodity, fixed income, multi-asset, and balanced mutual funds for its clients. It launches equity, fixed income, multi-asset, and balanced exchange-traded funds. The firm also launches and manages private funds. It invests in the public equity and fixed income markets across the globe. The firm prefers to invest between $5 million and $15 million in companies. The firm also invests in alternative markets, such as commodities and currencies. For the equity portion of its portfolio, it invests in growth and value stocks of large-cap, mid-cap, and small-cap companies. For the fixed income portion of its portfolio, the firm invests in convertibles, government bonds, municipal bonds, treasury securities, and cash. It also invests in short term and intermediate term bonds, investment grade and high yield bonds, taxable and tax-free bonds, senior secured loans, and structured securities such as asset-backed securities, mortgage-backed securities, and commercial mortgage-backed securities. The firm employs absolute return, global macro, and long/short strategies. It employs quantitative analysis to make its investments. The firm was formerly known as Invesco Plc, AMVESCAP plc, Amvesco plc, Invesco PLC, Invesco MIM, and H. Lotery & Co. Ltd. Invesco Ltd. was founded in 1935 and is based in Atlanta, Georgia with an additional office in Asia, Europe, Africa and North America.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Andrew Ryan Schlossberg | President, CEO & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $6.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $860K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $194K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Invesco Ltd is a large-cap financial services business with a $12.7B market cap on $6.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $1.4B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 23 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -8.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.8pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 40% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $7.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 59/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 36% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Invesco Advantage Municipal Income Trust II (NYSEAMERICAN:VKI) Stock Short Interest Report for October","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/invesco-advantage-municipal-income-trust-ii-nyseamericanvki-stock-short-interest-report-for-october.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794610882.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.982,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Invesco BulletShares 2030 Municipal Bond ETF (NASDAQ:BSMU) Shares Shorted: Short Interest Down 70.8% in October","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/invesco-bulletshares-2030-municipal-bond-etf-nasdaqbsmu-shares-shorted-short-interest-down-70-8-in-october.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794609703.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.942,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Invesco Mortgage Capital Inc. November 2026 Dividend Announcement and October Financial Update","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/real-estate/articles/invesco-mortgage-capital-inc-november-211500863.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794604500.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Peachtree Road Race updates: Healthy habits","source":"ajc.co